# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — the most important lines in this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds your real LINE channel token and secret. Anyone who gets that
# token can send messages as your bot. Once a secret is committed to git it
# stays in the history forever, even if you delete the file in a later commit,
# and this repo has to be PUBLIC because YOLO is AGPL-3.0.
#
# .env.example is the opposite: it contains only placeholders, so it IS
# committed — that is how a teammate knows which variables they need.
.env
.env.local
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Photos users send to the bot. Not source code, potentially private (people
# photograph their own kitchens), and they pile up quickly.
data/incoming/

# Trained YOLO weights from Person 1 — often 50MB+, too big for git.
*.pt

# Exported BERT NER model weights (models/bert_ner/) — same reason, too big
# for git. Config/tokenizer json files in that folder stay trackable.
*.safetensors
*.bin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch work
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Throwaway experimentation, not meant to enter permanent history.
Experiment/

# added 2026-10-02 (security audit)
*.pem
id_rsa*
credentials*
*.p12
*.pfx
tmp/
scratch/
